    <content:encoded>[caption id="attachment_1082" align="alignright" width="300"]&lt;a href="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2005/10/cockpit.jpg"&gt;&lt;img class="size-medium wp-image-1082" alt="Looking to turn at the shoreline of Santa Monica" src="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2005/10/cockpit.jpg?w=300" width="300" height="199" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Looking to turn at the shoreline of Santa Monica[/caption]

This blog will be a strange place. We'll use it as a flight log, but I plan on posting my musings about flying here, too. Right now it is just Adam and Colin. Maybe eventually passengers will have a comments area. "You call THAT a smooth landing? I'm glad I'm not in the plane for the ones you call rough."

(In the photo, I have two hands on the yoke. It was smooth air so that was bad form. The plane should mostly fly itself, I should just make small adjustments with a couple fingers of one hand.)</content:encoded>
